    "K_t": "Evidence:\n[1] Opened in 1959, the line climbs Mount Tenjō from the shores of Lake Kawaguchi, one of the Fuji Five Lakes.\n[2] The name Fuji Five Lakes comes from the fact that there are five lakes formed by previous eruptions of Mount Fuji.\n[3] Aokigahara (青木ヶ原 ) , also known as the Suicide Forest or Sea of Trees (樹海 , Jukai ) , is a forest on the northwestern flank of Japan's Mount Fuji thriving on 30 square kilometers (12 square miles) of hardened lava laid down by the last major eruption of Mount Fuji in 864 CE."
